# launchd jobs taken out of the macOS 15.6 (Sequoia, 24G84) root by tools/macos/sequoia-post.sh: configuration only
# (the entries move from /System/Library/xpc/launchd.plist to launchd-disabled.plist beside it, their plists are renamed
# *.starbite-off; nothing executable changes). Every label below was checked present in 15.6's launchd.plist (2026-11-11).
# WindowServer, loginwindow, opendirectoryd, securityd, logd, watchdogd stay IN.
#
# A. Likely to block the boot or panic it: each crash-looped on Ventura on the same 12377 macOS-target kernel
#    (evidence: tools/macos/ventura-smooth.list "crash loops", 2026-11-05; memory ventura-desktop-milestones).
com.apple.kernelmanagerd        # crash loop on Ventura; 15.6's job has _PanicOnCrash {PanicOnConsecutiveCrash}, so a
                                # loop = a panic (Ventura first had to strip _PanicOnCrash, then took the job out). This
                                # root has no /System/Library/{Extensions,KernelCollections} for it to manage.
                                # Driver plan: kext-management answers (Part 4). NOTE docs/MACOS.md 11.5: if
                                # IOKitWaitQuiet callers hang without it, put it back with root26-cycle --enable-job.
com.apple.audio.coreaudiod      # crash loop on Ventura: no audio device. Driver plan: null audio device (Part 3, #26)
com.apple.chronod               # crash loop on Ventura (widgets timeline daemon)
# 2026-11-05 04:15 (Ventura): speech-synthesis extensions and pivtoken (CryptoTokenKit) crash-looped, 600+ spawns a boot
